      "note": "### Investigation Steps\n1. Identify the internal host (`source.ip`) and owner. Is SSH/RDP egress via proxy expected for this user (sysadmin, researcher with external compute)?\n2. Check `destination.ip`, `destination.geo.country_name` and `destination.as.organization.name`. Cloud/VPS providers in unexpected countries deserve a closer look.\n3. Pivot on `source.ip` for the last 24h: how many distinct destinations on this port, total `source.bytes` (long-lived large tunnels suggest reverse shells or data transfer).\n4. Repeated connections at a fixed interval = possible beacon.\n\n### False positives\nAdministrators and research groups legitimately SSH to external servers. Add known admin hosts/destinations to an exception list rather than disabling the rule. Alerts are suppressed per source/destination/port for 12h.",
